    "description": "We are currently seeking a DevOps Engineer (m/f/d) specializing in F5 ALG, iRules & ICAP for our client. The position is expected to run until July 2027, with the option for long-term extension. This is a full-time role, primarily conducted remotely. Please note: Only submit an application if you meet all the must-have requirements and more than 80% of the nice-to-have criteria. Only projects ending within the last three years and with a minimum duration of six months will be considered. Responsibilities: - Conceptualization, setup, administration, and operation of network infrastructure components - Technical and technological consulting for product owners and software engineering teams regarding product and project requirements - Creation and maintenance of rule sets within F5 for ingress and egress - Consulting on the specification and design of complex network infrastructures with F5 ALGs - Consulting on the commissioning of complex network infrastructures with F5 ALGs - Administration of complex network infrastructures with F5 ALGs during operation - Process automation (continuous integration, continuous delivery, test automation) of F5 ALGs - Independent administration and configuration of F5 ALGs - System maintenance and support of network infrastructure components - Connection to monitoring systems and monitoring of assigned network infrastructure components - Setup, operation, and evaluation of fiber optic network taps to analyze data traffic for anomalies and attack patterns - Documentation of best practice approaches and support for knowledge sharing Must Have: - 2 years or 3 projects (min. 6 months per project) of experience in setting up or operating an application layer gateway from the manufacturer F5 Experience with the modules: WAF, LTM, and SSLO - 2 years or 3 projects (min. 6 months per project) in writing iRules, creating rule sets, SSL profiles (client/server), and evaluating event logs - Min. 6 months of experience in 1 project where the integration of ICAP in an F5 Proxy WAF environment was successfully implemented and operated - Min. 6 months of experience in Packet Capture and Deep Packet Inspection for analyzing network traffic via optical network taps - German C2 or native speaker - English B2 Nice to Have: - TCP and HTTP - Troubleshooting with TCP dumps and working on the CLI - Maintenance and administration of HA systems - Programming Infrastructure as a Code in Ansible and/or Python - Writing code for automation (creating rule sets, profiles) - Working in a critical infrastructure company/project - Experience with F5 BigIP modules: > F5 WAF > F5 LTM > F5 SSLO > F5 APM - Data traffic analysis via packet capture for anomaly/attack pattern analysis - Napatech capture cards and Netscout packet broker - Packet firewalls from Checkpoint Maestro, versions R81.20 and R82\n\nSkills: DevOps Engineer, F5, iRules, ICAP, Packet Capture",
